            <div xml:id="d1226">

                <pb facs="1088" n="774" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg774"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 867.00/722</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Morgenthau</hi>)</head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-12-01T22:00:00-05:00">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">December 1, 1914, 10 p.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>90. Your despatch 120, October 5.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1226-f1"/> Department
                    forwarded to the Navy Department copy of circular <hi rendition="#italic">note
                        verbale</hi> from the Sublime Porte and has received a reply from the Navy
                    Department suggesting in view of the limitations placed upon the cruising ground
                    of naval vessels in Turkish waters by the terms of this note, that the American
                    Ambassador be asked his opinion as to whether under the <pb facs="1089" n="775"
                        xml:id="pg775"/> circumstances one of the two United States warships now in
                    Ottoman waters might be returned to the United States. Each vessel was sent to
                    Europe hurriedly, and is in need of docking and repair.</p>
                <p>Please report to Department.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
